# Button cursor

Enabled buttons always use `cursor: pointer`. Disabled or `aria-disabled` buttons keep the default cursor.

This is set once in `apps/web/src/index.css` (`@layer base`). Do not add `cursor-pointer` on individual `<button>` elements.

```css
button:not(:disabled):not([aria-disabled="true"]) {
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

When a control is not a `<button>` but acts as one (`role="button"`, submit inputs), it follows the same rule.
